IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedules 3 and 4: the lists of disability payments that the text repeats.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- WHY A MODULE OF ITS OWN. The same list of seven payments is written out in Schedule 3 para 5(3)(b), Schedule 4 para 12(3)(a),
-- para 12(6A)(a) and para 15(2)(b) to (da); a list of two in para 12(6)(a); a list of six (without child disability payment) in para
-- 16(2)(c) to (ea), the same six in the "entitled but not receiving" limbs of paras 15(2)(e) and 16(2)(f); and a different list of six
-- (without pension age disability payment) in para 29(5). Schedule 4 (bedrooms, contributions) and Schedule 3 both read them, and a name defined in two modules cannot be used, so the lists are written once here, each rule named for
-- the first place the text writes the list. Whether a person receives (or is entitled to) a payment is a stated input: the rates,
-- components and the Regulations that suspend payment on admission to hospital are not among the inputs.

-- A person's position on one payment: receiving it, entitled to it but not receiving it under the regulation that paras 15(2)(e) and 16(2)(f)
-- list for that payment (suspension on admission to hospital or the like), or neither.
-- src:2332 | (e) a person who is entitled to a payment within paragraph (b) , (bb) , (c) , (ca), (d) or (da) but is not receiving it under, as the case may be—
-- src:2333 | (i) regulation 8 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2334 | (ii) regulation 6 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2335 | (iii) regulation 21 of the Social Security (General Benefit) Regulations 1982, ...
-- src:2336 | (iv) regulations under section 86 of the Act (payment of personal independence payment while a person is a hospital in-patient) ...;
-- src:2337 | (v) regulation 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 , ...
-- src:2338 | (vi) regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024 , or
-- src:2339 | (vii) regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) (src:2332-2339)
DECLARE `Status of a disability payment` IS ONE OF
    `received by the person`
    `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`
    `neither received nor so entitled`

-- The seven payments of Schedule 3 para 5(3)(b), written in the same order in the other paragraphs.
-- src:2087 | (3) A person is specified in this sub-paragraph if the person is—
-- src:2088 | (a) a claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible; and
-- src:2089 | (b) in receipt of—
-- src:2090 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate,
-- src:2091 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations,
-- src:2092 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025,
-- src:2093 | (ii) attendance allowance, ...
-- src:2094 | (iia) pension age disability payment,
-- src:2095 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment or
-- src:2096 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate
@ref Sch 3 para 5(3) (src:2087-2096)
DECLARE `Disability payments of a person` HAS
    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate`    IS A `Status of a disability payment`
    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations`  IS A `Status of a disability payment`
    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025`  IS A `Status of a disability payment`
    `attendance allowance`                                                           IS A `Status of a disability payment`
    `pension age disability payment`                                                 IS A `Status of a disability payment`
    `daily living component of personal independence payment`                        IS A `Status of a disability payment`
    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate`  IS A `Status of a disability payment`

-- "In receipt of" one of the seven. Same list in Sch 4 para 12(3)(a), para 12(6A)(a) and para 15(2)(b) to (da).
-- src:2090 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate,
-- src:2091 | (ia) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations,
-- src:2092 | (ib) the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025,
-- src:2093 | (ii) attendance allowance, ...
-- src:2094 | (iia) pension age disability payment,
-- src:2095 | (iii) the daily living component of personal independence payment or
-- src:2096 | (iv) the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate
@ref Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) (src:2090-2096)
GIVEN payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 para 5(3)(b) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` payments MEANS
    (payments's `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `attendance allowance` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `pension age disability payment` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `daily living component of personal independence payment` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` EQUALS `received by the person`)

-- Para 12(6)(a): a child in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance or of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate.
-- src:2287 | (a) in receipt of—
-- src:2288 | (i) the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate; or
-- src:2289 | (ii) the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations; and
@ref Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) (src:2287-2289)
GIVEN payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 12(6)(a) — a child in receipt of one of the listed care components` payments MEANS
    (payments's `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` EQUALS `received by the person`)

-- Para 16(2)(c) to (ea): six of the seven (child disability payment is not among them).
-- src:2345 | (c) a person in receipt of the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate;
-- src:2346 | (ca) a person in receipt of the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate;
-- src:2347 | (d) a person in receipt of attendance allowance;
-- src:2348 | (da) a person in receipt of pension age disability payment;
-- src:2349 | (e) a person in receipt of the daily living component of personal independence payment;
-- src:2350 | (ea) a person in receipt of the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate;
@ref Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) (src:2345-2350)
GIVEN payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 16(2)(c) to (ea) — a person in receipt of one of the listed payments` payments MEANS
    (payments's `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `attendance allowance` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `pension age disability payment` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `daily living component of personal independence payment` EQUALS `received by the person`)
    OR (payments's `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` EQUALS `received by the person`)

-- Paras 15(2)(e) and 16(2)(f): entitled to a payment within the six but not receiving it under the regulation listed for it. Child disability
-- payment is not in the list of paragraph 15(2)(e) ("(b), (bb), (c), (ca), (d) or (da)") nor in that of paragraph 16(2)(f).
-- src:2332 | (e) a person who is entitled to a payment within paragraph (b) , (bb) , (c) , (ca), (d) or (da) but is not receiving it under, as the case may be—
-- src:2333 | (i) regulation 8 of the Social Security (Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2334 | (ii) regulation 6 of the Social Security (Attendance Allowance) Regulations 1991,
-- src:2335 | (iii) regulation 21 of the Social Security (General Benefit) Regulations 1982, ...
-- src:2336 | (iv) regulations under section 86 of the Act (payment of personal independence payment while a person is a hospital in-patient) ...;
-- src:2337 | (v) regulation 28 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Adult Disability Payment) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022 , ...
-- src:2338 | (vi) regulation 20 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to pension age disability payment) of the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024 , or
-- src:2339 | (vii) regulation 23 (effect of admission to hospital on ongoing entitlement to Scottish adult disability living allowance) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025.
@ref Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) (src:2332-2339)
GIVEN payments IS A `Disability payments of a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 15(2)(e) — a person entitled to one of the listed payments but not receiving it` payments MEANS
    (payments's `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` EQUALS `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`)
    OR (payments's `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` EQUALS `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`)
    OR (payments's `attendance allowance` EQUALS `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`)
    OR (payments's `pension age disability payment` EQUALS `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`)
    OR (payments's `daily living component of personal independence payment` EQUALS `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`)
    OR (payments's `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` EQUALS `entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it`)

-- Para 29(5): six payments, a different six from paragraph 16(2): child disability payment is in this list and pension age disability payment is not.
-- src:2487 | (5) E is under 35 years old and is in receipt of—
